WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.411
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Lion's Breath.

00:00:14.411 --> 00:00:20.822
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:20.822 --> 00:00:24.668
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:24.668 --> 00:00:28.515
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:28.515 --> 00:00:37.490
This is a breathing practice with a playful shape. You breathe in through your nose. Then you let the breath out as a soft lion roar.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:47.747
The roar sounds like this: mouth open, tongue out, and a quiet "haaa." It is a breath wearing a lion costume — not a shout, and never a scream. Lion-cub volume.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:59.287
The roar goes out into the room's air — never at a person. And nobody has to roar. A quiet sigh out is the same practice, whole and complete.

00:00:59.287 --> 00:01:04.416
Nothing is ever held. The air moves in, the air moves out. That is the whole shape. Here we go.

00:01:04.416 --> 00:01:15.955
Round one. Breathe in through your nose… and roar it out, soft and quiet: haaa.

00:01:15.955 --> 00:01:27.495
Round two. In through your nose… tongue out, and let it go: haaa.

00:01:27.495 --> 00:01:39.035
Round three. In… and out with your lion breath: haaa. Let your shoulders drop as the roar rolls away.

00:01:39.035 --> 00:01:49.292
Round four. In through your nose… and one more soft roar: haaa.

00:01:49.292 --> 00:01:50.574
One last round, your own way. Roar softly, or sigh it out — both are the practice. Then let the roaring go, and just breathe the way your body wants to.

00:01:50.574 --> 00:02:02.114
Now hear the rules that keep this practice yours. The shape is a gentle guide — it is never a test.

00:02:02.114 --> 00:02:13.653
A smaller, quieter roar is a complete practice. Your breath, your pace. And this is never a contest — not the loudest, not the longest, not the biggest.

00:02:13.653 --> 00:02:22.629
And if anything ever feels dizzy, or tight, or strange, the move is simple: breathe normally. Normal breathing is always allowed, at any second. It is never a failure.

00:02:22.629 --> 00:02:23.911
Notice how your breathing feels now, all on its own. Nothing to fix. Nothing to hold.

00:02:23.911 --> 00:02:32.886
In through your nose. Out with a soft roar. Then let it be.

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:39.297
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:39.297 --> 00:02:44.426
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:44.426 --> 00:02:50.836
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:57.247
You're ready for what's next.
